# 5. Recommended footprint design

## Target operating model

### Existing East Asian hub

Retain:

- Product engineering;
- Core technology;
- Proprietary and safety-critical components;
- Master tooling;
- Early-stage prototypes;
- Complex engineering-to-order products;
- Supplier qualification leadership; and
- Global process standards.

Reduce concentration over time in:

- Standardized final assembly;
- Commodity fabrication;
- Routine subassembly;
- Regional configuration;
- Common replacement parts; and
- ASEAN-bound production.

### Thailand regional hub

Develop:

- Complex final assembly;
- Machining;
- Welded and fabricated structures;
- System integration;
- Factory acceptance testing;
- Supplier-development center;
- Regional spare-parts stock;
- Manufacturing engineering; and
- Training academy for ASEAN plants.

### Vietnam second production platform

Develop:

- Standard product families;
- Labor-intensive assembly;
- Electrical and mechanical subassemblies;
- Fabrication and enclosure work;
- Export programs;
- Capacity overflow; and
- Lower-cost production cells.

### Malaysia specialist center

Evaluate for:

- Controls;
- Precision electronics;
- Test equipment;
- Calibration;
- Digital manufacturing support;
- Product lifecycle data management; and
- Regional technical support.

### Indonesia and Philippines

Use initially for:

- Local-market assembly;
- Service and refurbishment;
- Customer configuration;
- Engineering support;
- Spare parts;
- Field installation; and
- Targeted product programs.

